    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d0048ff8_843fba8f",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/LinkProperties.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 905,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-25T03:44:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What should happen if the passed prefix is a sub-prefix of one that\u0027s already assigned ? What if it includes completely one that\u0027s already assigned ?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 905,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 905,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "32a16a7e9fe0311b1696ce3d53e276fef896f487",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d2c83af_4f903091",
        "filename": "framework/src/android/net/LinkProperties.java",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 905,
      "author": {
        "id": 1406251
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-01-09T02:26:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "per discussion on the standup, given the prefix is added by the caller(e.g. IpClient gets it from DHCPv6 PD) then we can keep the prefix as-is and put it to the set even it might be a sub-prefix of one that\u0027s already assigned, we can treat them as two different prefixes (i.e. the prefix length is not identical).",
      "parentUuid": "d0048ff8_843fba8f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 905,
        "startChar": 19,
        "endLine": 905,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "32a16a7e9fe0311b1696ce3d53e276fef896f487",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
